From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:15:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] backlight: ktz8869_iceland: Start at stock's default
 brightness

The driver registered the backlight at 2047 of 4095, half the range,
so a system without a saved brightness (the first boot of a new
install) came up much brighter than stock: 4095 was seen at first use,
9.2 W against 2.2-3.0 W at stock's level.

Start at stock's default instead: SettingsProvider's
def_screen_brightness is 102 of 255 on stock's manual range, which ends
at level 3542 of the same 12-bit scale (above it is the HBM range):
3542 * 102 / 255 = 1417. From the second boot on userspace restores the
user's own value as before.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
index 8930f570fc68..a8de2dbd2e4a 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
@@ -14,7 +14,11 @@
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/thermal.h>
 
-#define DEFAULT_BRIGHTNESS 2047
+/*
+ * Stock's default brightness: SettingsProvider def_screen_brightness 102
+ * of 255 on stock's manual range, which ends at level 3542 (HBM above).
+ */
+#define DEFAULT_BRIGHTNESS 1417
 #define MAX_BRIGHTNESS 4095
 #define REG_MAX 0x15
 
